  "limits": [
    "The original user device was not profiled here. The native clock sampled about165Hz and shows no old/new pacing improvement; the verified60Hz bug is not proof of the cause of all real-world stutters.",
    "The0.1ms tolerance is phase preserving and bounded; tests cover fixed refresh rates and0.1ms rounding for60seconds. Arbitrary jitter, coarser clocks, all initial phases and long-session numerical error are not fully verified.",
    "On affected60Hz clocks the fix restores intended render submissions from2983 to3600 per minute in the controlled model. More correct draws can increase work compared with the buggy under-rendering; reducedGPU or CPU use is not guaranteed.",
    "75Hz has ordinary display-cycle quantization gaps of26.667ms at a60fps cap; this patch does not remove that behavior or raise the cap.",
    "The tool rejected a60000ms native press before sending input. Two30second holds per leg have270.79/275.05ms moving-packet gaps and are explicitly segmented regression gameplay. Strict continuous60seconds remains unaccepted.",
    "The final1920x1080/DPR1.5 page retained10/10 slow records, including cold ground121.6ms within draw123.7ms; maxRAF186.9ms remains. Five initial records are a prefix of the final ten. New samples have endpoint/farm positions, which alone cannot prove motion state.",
    "No full-frame percentile, physical presentation, GPU usage, browser total800MB, long-memory or uninstrumented performance comparison is claimed. The observer adds diagnostic logging/copying overhead; JS heap is a single distinct metric.",
    "Native final screenshot/AX precede final server checkpoint; satiety naturally differs. No GM, coordinate, inventory, health or clock edits were used.",
    "Normal source push is not deployment of the external website. The complete exploration, multiplayer camp, economy and performance goal remains active."
  ],
